# Trivy suppressions — see .github/workflows/ci.yml.
# Format: one advisory ID per line; lines starting with # are comments.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy Streamlit manifest (requirements.txt)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-25087 — Apache Arrow C++ use-after-free DoS on malicious Arrow IPC
# input. Via pyarrow==15.0.0 in requirements.txt (the Streamlit Community Cloud
# manifest only). Not exploitable here: the dashboard reads its own trusted
# parquet, never attacker-supplied Arrow IPC. requirements.txt is not used by
# CI, the API, or the image, and is deleted in deployment_stages.md Phase 9.
# Re-evaluate at Phase 1 task 8 (bump / retire requirements.txt).
CVE-2026-25087

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base-image packaging tooling (python:3.11-slim, /usr/local Python)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The runtime app runs from /opt/venv; the packages below live in the base
# image's *system* Python (pip / setuptools / wheel and pip's vendored bundle)
# and are never invoked by `uvicorn api.main:app`. Proper fix is Phase 1 task 4:
# digest-pin the base image and strip/upgrade its build tooling in the runtime
# stage.
# jaraco.context (setuptools vendor) — path traversal via malicious tar
CVE-2026-23949
# msgpack (pip vendor) — out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
# setuptools PackageIndex — path traversal
CVE-2025-47273
# wheel — privilege escalation / code execution via malicious wheel file
CVE-2026-24049
